Print one variable's value, without sourcing the file.

The value is printed alone, so `PORT=$(evnx get PORT)` works. It is read as `evnx run` would pass it on: quotes removed, escapes resolved, `${NAME}` expanded.

A name that looks secret (`API_TOKEN`, `DB_PASSWORD`), or a value that looks like a credential, is refused without --reveal, also when the output is piped. `evnx get NAME --exists` prints nothing and says in the exit code whether the name is there, secret or not.

A name that is not in the file exits 1.

Usage: evnx get [OPTIONS] <NAME>

Arguments:
  <NAME>
          The variable to print

Options:
      --exists
          Print nothing; exit 0 when the name is in the file, 1 when it is not

      --reveal
          Print the value even when the name looks secret

      --no-color
          Disable colored output

  -q, --quiet
          Print nothing on success. Findings, warnings, errors and requested data still print

  -v, --verbose
          Enable verbose output

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version

Files:
      --env <FILE>
          Env file to use. Defaults to `.env`

      --env-name <NAME>
          Use `.env.<NAME>` instead of `.env`

  -C, --dir <DIR>
          Project folder to work in. Defaults to the current folder

Output:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format
          
          [default: pretty]
          [possible values: pretty, json]

      --json
          Print the result as JSON. A secret value is left out unless --reveal.

Examples:
  PORT=$(evnx get PORT)                     one value, no sourcing
  evnx get --exists DATABASE_URL            exit 0 when set, 1 when not; prints nothing
  evnx get API_TOKEN --reveal               a secret is printed only on request
  evnx get PORT --env-name staging          from .env.staging

Exit codes:
    0  Ran, nothing to report
    1  Ran, and found something: findings, problems, a difference, not in sync
    2  Could not run: usage, config, I/O, or refused before any change
    4  Declined: answered no, or a confirmation was needed with no terminal and no --yes
  141  Output closed early (broken pipe)

Full guide: https://docs.evnx.dev/cli/commands/get
